# FULL TOOLFACTORY API-BASE PARITY DRIVE (operator: "keep extending until we can get full toolfactory api base parity,
# minus the Tools routes transcribe and convert"). autotoolfactory (the generated app) → the SAME /api surface + middleware
# stack + contract + MCP as toolfactory, EXCLUDING the two product routes (/api/transcribe + /api/subtitle/convert). The
# parity ORACLE is /home/mk/apps/toolfactory/api/src (43 /api routes + a 6-layer /api/* middleware stack). Governed by C052
# (own the wiring, npm the logic — zero new packages).

# THE MEASURED PLAN (5-agent map + synthesis over the real code): 6 DEPENDENCY-ORDERED WAVES, newPackagesNeeded = ZERO
# (only install already-published deps @suluk/mcp + @suluk/reference). Already-covered by the 13 services: auth, credits
# (+transactions), keys(+provision/revoke), logs, cost, erasure, email, rate-limit, webhooks, journeys, audit, health.
# WAVES: (1) app-base cors + identity + apiKeyAuth middleware + the CONTRACT keystone; (2) enforceApiKeyScope + validation +
# reference + admin/stats + rate-credit + logquery + bulk; (3) billing completeness (~14 routes); (4) MCP auth foundation
# (Better Auth mcp() plugin + oauth tables); (5) MCP surface (bearer + server mount + connections + consent); (6) conformance
# + journeys artifact wiring + final parity proof. The CONTRACT is the keystone — toolfactory is contract-first (RouteContracts
# via @suluk/hono declare each op with x-suluk-access/-cost/-ratelimit facets; the doc + scope-gate + validation + mcp all
# DERIVE from it). measured-not-yet-fully-built => ceiling 0.5.
claim parity_drive_measured_6_wave_plan_zero_new_packages: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when parity_drive_measured_6_wave_plan_zero_new_packages == False

# WAVE 1 DONE + PROVEN (2026-07-01). (1a) the /api/* MIDDLEWARE FOUNDATION that grounds the scoped-caller model (rate-limit
# was inert — nothing set c.get("user")): app gained cors on /api/* (trusted-origin allowlist from env, credentials:true,
# never "*") + /api/health; auth gained identity(roleScopes) (getSession once per /api/*, set user+scopes, skip /api/auth+
# anon, degrade-to-anonymous) + apiKeyAuth (x-api-key -> verifyApiKey -> same slots + keyId) over @suluk/better-auth
# (principalFromSession + verifyApiKey), both installed by mountAuthRoutes on /api/*. Real-context tsc caught 2 bugs (a
# SessionLike cast; VerifyApiKeyResult is a FLAT interface so res.ok doesn't narrow -> guard res.key?.userId). (1b) the
# CONTRACT keystone (built via a grounded workflow: builder + adversarial verifier): CONTRACT = contractDoc([...base ops with
# x-suluk-access scopes...]); apiDocument(principal?) via emitV4 (per-principal doc projection); SCOPE_BY_OP + PUBLIC_OPS
# DERIVED from CONTRACT (the Wave-2 scope gate + the MCP tool-gate consume them, so they can't drift); GET /api/openapi.json
# projects to c.get("scopes") (anonymous -> public surface, defaults to []); declares the apiKey security scheme. Over
# @suluk/hono (npm the emitV4 derivation). (1c) /api/* ROUTE ALIGNMENT: catalog feature paths shifted /credits->/api/credits
# etc. so the /api/* middleware covers them (toolfactory parity); contract mounts at /api. @suluk/platform 0.1.4 (published);
# two-pass buildEntry keeps middleware before routes. VALIDATED: platform tests 14 pass; shadcn build ok (15 items); the
# 15-service autotoolfactory regenerated BYTE-IDENTICAL from the installed 0.1.4 generator, tsc = 0 own-code errors
# (autotoolfactory 24936b0). OPEN (Wave 2): the contract declares idealized paths (/api/credits) while modules expose
# /api/credits/balance/:userId — the scope gate's path->op resolver reconciles this.
claim parity_drive_wave1_middleware_foundation_plus_contract_keystone_api_aligned: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when parity_drive_wave1_middleware_foundation_plus_contract_keystone_api_aligned == False

# WAVE 2 (mostly) DONE + PROVEN (2026-07-01). (2a) the SCOPE GATE `enforceApiKeyScope` — the piece that makes the scoped-
# caller model ENFORCE: scopeForRequest(method,path) resolves a request to its contract op by LONGEST static-prefix +
# method (a module sub-path /api/credits/balance/x -> the getCredits op at /api/credits; GET->:read POST->:write) —
# RECONCILING the contract's idealized paths with the modules' real route shapes; a keyed caller (keyId set) missing the
# op's scope gets 403 (RFC-9457 via @suluk/core toProblemDetails), sessions pass through. The contract module became a
# MIDDLEWARE mount `mountContract(app)` installing the gate on /api/* + GET /api/openapi.json (both contract-derived),
# placed after auth. Real-context tsc caught a bug (c.get("scopes") on a generic app types the key as `never` -> read via
# c.var cast). (2b) THREE modules built in parallel (workflow: builder + adversarial verifier): `reference` (over
# @suluk/reference + the contract's apiDocument) — GET /api/reference renders the derived v4 doc, /api/reference/:tool
# projects to one op; registryDep contract; derived/stateless. `admin` (over @suluk/credits ledgerStats) — GET
# /api/admin/stats (admin-scoped by the gate) + module-owned credit_transaction count; stateless read. `logquery` (EXTENDS
# logs, fully-owned) — GET /api/logs/query, a parameterized filter DSL (whitelist fields + bound drizzle params + LIKE-
# escape; the verifier PROVED an injection payload becomes an inert bound `?`). Registry now 17 items. @suluk/platform 0.1.5
# published. VALIDATED: platform tests 15 pass; shadcn build ok (17); the 17-service autotoolfactory regenerated BYTE-
# IDENTICAL from the installed 0.1.5 generator (middleware order mountAuthRoutes; mountContract[gate]; mountRateLimit;
# mountI18n; THEN routes incl /api/reference + /api/admin), tsc = 0 own-code errors (autotoolfactory 4b154ec). DEFERRED to
# Wave 2c: validation (contract request-schemas + a derived validate middleware) + rate-credit (the µ$ free-tier bucket —
# large; the fixed-window rate-limit already provides the abuse cap for base parity). bulk skipped (its only oracle consumer
# is the excluded subtitle route).
claim parity_drive_wave2_scope_gate_reference_admin_logquery_proven: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when parity_drive_wave2_scope_gate_reference_admin_logquery_proven == False

# WAVE 3 DONE + PROVEN — BILLING COMPLETENESS (2026-07-01). Extended the billing module from 5 flows to the FULL
# /api/billing/* surface (~14 new routes -> 23 total), built by ONE deeply-grounded agent (money-critical, one cohesive
# module = one context) + an adversarial verifier that PASSED all 6 money checks (correct @suluk/billing call signatures,
# refund-debits-before-refunding, idempotent grants, parameterized owned tables, transpiles). billing.pricing.ts (OWNED per
# C052 — pricing is app POLICY): CREDIT_PACKS + SUB_PLANS + quote math (COGS 450µ$/markup 73/tier-discounts/creditsForUsd/
# refundNetCents) ported from toolfactory pricing.ts; client sends only a pack/plan id, amounts server-authoritative. Routes
# wire VERIFIED @suluk/billing exports (createCheckout, createSubscriptionOnDefaultCard, getSubscriptionStatus,
# setSubscriptionCancel, changeSubscriptionPlan, createPaymentIntent[OnDefaultCard], listPaymentMethods/setDefault/detach/
# ownsPaymentMethod, calculateTax, upsertBillingAccount, ...): packs/plans/payment-config/checkout/payment-intent/subscribe/
# subscription[get,cancel]/subscription-plan/purchase-quote/refund-quote/refund/methods[default,delete]/auto-topup[get,set]/
# payment-health. REFUND is MODULE-OWNED (@suluk/billing EXCLUDES refund): ports ~50 LoC of Stripe-refund primitives via the
# stripePost/stripeGet transport — DEBITS credits BEFORE moving cash, refunds netCents across the customer's succeeded
# charges newest-first (each idempotent + partial-capped at Stripe's headroom -> can't over-refund), re-credits any shortfall
# via grantOnce. OWNED tables auto_topup + payment_alert (0006_billing_v2 migration, drizzle-parameterized). SECURITY FIX on
# integration: the money routes' caller() now reads the AUTHENTICATED principal (c.get("user"), set by the Wave-1 identity
# middleware) via a c.var cast — NEVER a client-supplied x-user-id (the builder's placeholder would have let a caller move
# ANYONE's money). +@suluk/credits +drizzle-orm billing deps. VALIDATED: 5 billing files transpile; shadcn build ok (17
# items); the extended billing type-checks in autotoolfactory against real @suluk/billing + @suluk/credits = 0 own-code
# errors (Context.Tag.Service typing + caller + all signatures). NO platform republish/regen (billing catalog UNCHANGED —
# same /api/billing mount); re-shadcn-add billing -> 23 routes, tsc 0 own-code errors (autotoolfactory d255fd5). KNOWN
# follow-ups (not money bugs): refund uses debitCredits (pre-guarded by getBalance; a race -> 500 no-money-moved; debitIfCovers
# would be atomic); the maybeAutoTopup BACKGROUND trigger isn't ported (the config surface is — the trigger is a cron the app
# wires). SCOPE-GATE HARDENING (found during Wave 3 integration): the gate matched only DECLARED contract ops, so a keyed
# caller hitting an UNDECLARED billing sub-path (POST /api/billing/refund /subscribe /auto-topup, GET /subscription /quotes
# /methods) matched nothing -> was NOT gated (a real hole). Fixed scopeForRequest to TWO tiers: (1) exact longest-prefix op
# (declared public ops packs/plans stay public), then (2) a MODULE fallback — an undeclared /api/<module> sub-path is gated
# by that module's namespace scope (write scope for a write method, else read). Verified: refund/subscribe/auto-topup ->
# billing:write, subscription -> billing:read, packs/plans -> public, non-contract -> no gate. REMAINING: Waves 4-5 the MCP
# suite (oauth) + Wave 6 the parity proof.
claim parity_drive_wave3_billing_completeness_14_routes_proven: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when parity_drive_wave3_billing_completeness_14_routes_proven == False
